 done."}, {"ref": "Luke 22:43", "text": "And there appeared to him an angel from heaven, strengthening him. And being in an agony, he prayed the longer."}, {"ref": "Luke 22:44", "text": "And his sweat became as drops of blood, trickling down upon the ground."}, {"ref": "Luke 22:45", "text": "And when he rose up from prayer and was come to the disciples, he found them sleeping for sorrow."}, {"ref": "Luke 22:46", "text": "And he said to them: Why sleep you? Arise: pray: lest you enter into temptation."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:1", "text": "And it came to pass, when Jesus had ended all these words, he said to his disciples:"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:2", "text": "You know that after two days shall be the pasch: and the Son of man shall be delivered up to be crucified."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:3", "text": "Then were gathered together the chief priests and ancients of the people, into the court of the high priest, who was called Caiphas:"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:4", "text": "And they consulted together that by subtilty they might apprehend Jesus and put him to death."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:5", "text": "But they said: Not on the festival day, lest perhaps there should be a tumult among the people."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:6", "text": "And when Jesus was in Bethania, in the house of Simon the leper,"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:7", "text": "There came to him a woman having an alabaster box of precious ointment and poured it on his head as he was at table."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:8", "text": "And the disciples seeing it had indignation, saying: To what purpose is this waste?"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:9", "text": "For this might have been sold for much and given to the poor."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:10", "text": "And Jesus knowing it, said to them: Why do you trouble this woman? For she hath wrought a good work upon me."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:11", "text": "For the poor you have always with you: but me you have not always."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:12", "text": "For she in pouring this ointment on my body hath done it for my burial."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:13", "text": "Amen I say to you, wheresoever this gospel shall be preached in the whole world, that also which she hath done shall be told for a memory of her."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:14", "text": "Then went one of the twelve, who was called Judas Iscariot, to the chief priests."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:15", "text": "And said to them: What will you give me, and I will deliver him unto you? But they appointed him thirty pieces of silver."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:16", "text": "And from thenceforth he sought opportunity to betray him."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:17", "text": "And on the first day of the Azymes, the disciples came to Jesus, saying: Where wilt thou that we prepare for thee to eat the pasch?"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:18", "text": "But Jesus said: Go ye into the city to a certain man and say to him: The master saith, My time is near at hand. With thee I make the pasch with my disciples."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:19", "text": "And the disciples did as Jesus appointed to them: and they prepared the pasch."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:20", "text": "But when it was evening, he sat down with his twelve disciples."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:21", "text": "And whilst they were eating, he said: Amen I say to you that one of you is about to betray me."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:22", "text": "And they being very much troubled began every one to say: Is it I, Lord?"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:23", "text": "But he answering said: He that dippeth his hand with me in the dish, he shall betray me."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:24", "text": "The Son of man indeed goeth, as it is written of him. But woe to that man by whom the Son of man shall be betrayed. It were better for him, if that man had not been born."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:25", "text": "And Judas that betrayed him answering, said: Is it I, Rabbi? He saith to him: Thou hast said it."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:26", "text": "And whilst they were at supper, Jesus took bread and blessed and broke and gave to his disciples and said: Take ye and eat. This is my body."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:27", "text": "And taking the chalice, he gave thanks and gave to them, saying: Drink ye all of this."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:28", "text": "For this is my blood of the new testament, which shall be shed for many unto remission of sins."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:29", "text": "And I say to you, I will not drink from henceforth of this fruit of the vine until that day when I shall drink it with you new in the kingdom of my Father."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:30", "text": "And a hymn being said, they went out unto mount Olivet."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:31", "text": "Then Jesus saith to them: All you shall be scandalized in me this night. For it is written: I will strike the shepherd: and the sheep of the flock shall be dispersed."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:32", "text": "But after I shall be risen again, I will go before you into Galilee."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:33", "text": "And Peter answering, said to him: Although all shall be scandalized in thee, I will never be scandalized."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:34", "text": "Jesus said to him: Amen I say to thee that in this night before the cock crow, thou wilt deny me thrice."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:35", "text": "Peter saith to him: Yea, though I should die with thee, I will not deny thee. And in like manner said all the disciples."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:36", "text": "Then Jesus came with them into a country place which is called Gethsemani. And he said to his disciples: Sit you here, till I go yonder and pray."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:37", "text": "And taking with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, he began to grow sorrowful and to be sad."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:38", "text": "Then he saith to them: My soul is sorrowful even unto death. Stay you here and watch with me."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:39", "text": "And going a little further, he fell upon his face, praying and saying: My Father, if it be possible, let this chalice pass from me. Nevertheless, not as I will but as thou wilt."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:40", "text": "And he cometh to his disciples and findeth them asleep. And he saith to Peter: What? Could you not watch one hour with me?"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:41", "text": "Watch ye: and pray that ye enter not into temptation. The spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:42", "text": "Again the second time, he went and prayed, saying: My Father, if this chalice may not pass away, but I must drink it, thy will be done."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:43", "text": "And he cometh again and findeth them sleeping: for their eyes were heavy."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:44", "text": "And leaving them, he went again: and he prayed the third time, saying the selfsame word."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:45", "text": "Then he cometh to his disciples and said to them: Sleep ye now and take your rest. Behold the hour is at hand: and the Son of man shall be betrayed into the hands of sinners."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:46", "text": "Rise: let us go. Behold he is at hand that will betray me."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:47", "text": "As he yet spoke, behold Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great multitude with swords and clubs, sent from the chief priests and the ancients of the people."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:48", "text": "And he that betrayed him gave them a sign, saying: Whomsoever I shall kiss, that is he. Hold him fast."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:49", "text": "And forthwith coming to Jesus, he said: Hail, Rabbi. And he kissed him."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:50", "text": "And Jesus said to him: Friend, whereto art thou come? Then they came up and laid hands on Jesus and held him."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:51", "text": "And behold one of them that were with Jesus, stretching forth his hand, drew out his sword: and striking the servant of the high priest, cut off his ear."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:52", "text": "Then Jesus saith to him: Put up again thy sword into its place: for all that take the sword shall perish with the sword."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:53", "text": "Thinkest thou that I cannot ask my Father, and he will give me presently more than twelve legions of angels?"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:54", "text": "How then shall the scriptures be fulfilled, that so it must be done?"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:55", "text": "In that same hour, Jesus said to the multitudes: You are come out, as it were to a robber, with swords and clubs to apprehend me. I sat daily with you, teaching in the temple: and you laid not hands on me."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:56", "text": "Now all this was done that the scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled. Then the disciples, all leaving him, fled."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:57", "text": "But they holding Jesus led him to Caiphas the high priest, where the scribes and the ancients were assembled."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:58", "text": "And Peter followed him afar off, even to the court of the high priest, And going in, he sat with the servants, that he might see the end."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:59", "text": "And the chief priests and the whole council sought false witness against Jesus, that they might put him to death."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:60", "text": "And they found not, whereas many false witnesses had come in. And last of all there came two false witnesses:"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:61", "text": "And they said: This man said, I am able to destroy the temple of God and after three days to rebuild it."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:62", "text": "And the high priest rising up, said to him: Answerest thou nothing to the things which these witness against thee?"}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:63", "text": "But Jesus held his peace. And the high priest said to him: I adjure thee by the living God, that thou tell us if thou be the Christ the Son of God."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:64", "text": "Jesus saith to him: Thou hast said it. Nevertheless I say to you, hereafter you shall see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of the power of God and coming in the clouds of heaven."}, {"ref": "Matthew 26:65", "text"